//! task: fix
//! ask: Map a u8 to a score using `discerne`, without a default arm.
//! expect: EXS-E0351
//! refs: §8.5
//! explain: A scalar scrutinee's value space is 2^N, so no list of literal arms is exhaustive; the catch-all `aliter` is the only way. There is no machine fix, because the body of the default arm is the author's.

publica functio puncta(m: u8) -> u8 {
    discerne m {
        casus 1 { redde 10; }
        casus 2 { redde 20; }
    }
}
//@ fixed
publica functio puncta(m: u8) -> u8 {
    discerne m {
        casus 1 { redde 10; }
        casus 2 { redde 20; }
        aliter  { redde 0; }
    }
}
